# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Backup / scratch
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig

# Raw image media (per D101 template ground rule —
# only promoted+renamed images get committed)
documentation/**/images/_raw/

# asimov-design-review notes — a disposable cache asimov-design consumes and
# deletes (d101-feature-design-definition §4.10, D101-design-stage.html R10–R11). Not a design
# artifact; committing it would duplicate a PR's own review thread.
documentation/features/*.review.md

# Spec-stage validation sidecar — the last run's reports and default-taken
# assumptions, written by asimov-spec and overwritten by
# the next run (s101-implementation-plan-definition §9, D101-spec-stage.html §6.8).
# A cache, never a record; the assumptions themselves live in the S101.
documentation/specs/*/S101-*.review.md
# Design cache — a design that is not a file in the repo (a ticket thread),
# normalised into the shape the S101 definition §9 fixes, for the blind validation
# reader. The source's tool is the record; asimov-spec rewrites this on every
# run (S101 definition §3.1, §9).
documentation/specs/*/design.md

# Claude Code local state
.claude/settings.local.json

# SDD working directory (ledger, task briefs, large diff files)
.superpowers/

# SDD specs and plans — working documents that drive a change, not toolkit
# content. They belong to the session that produced them, not to the repo.
docs/superpowers/
